<main class="content">
<section class="reveal" id="profile">
<div class="section-kicker">01. Executive Summary</div>
<h2 class="section-title">OT Cybersecurity Leadership for Critical and Regulated Environments</h2>
<div class="executive-profile-wrap">
<div class="executive-copy">
<p class="executive-lead">Arun Rajagopal is a senior OT cybersecurity and industrial cybersecurity expert with more than 25 years of experience across industrial automation, control systems, cyber security consulting, architecture, programme delivery and business leadership.</p>
<p>His experience spans the full operating context of industrial cybersecurity: from PLC, SCADA, DCS and safety systems through to cyber strategy, regulatory assurance, security transformation and executive decision support.</p>
<p>He has held Head of Cyber Security, Managing Principal Consultant, Principal OT Cyber Security Consultant, Security Architect, Delivery Manager and Department Manager responsibilities, alongside commercial ownership covering P&amp;L, recruitment, proposals, client relationships and delivery.</p>
<p>This combination allows him to connect engineering reality, cyber risk, regulation, commercial priorities and delivery, particularly in environments where security must coexist with safety, availability and operational continuity.</p>
</div>
<aside class="card executive-role-card">
<div class="meta">Selected Leadership Roles</div>
<div class="role-stack"><span>Head of Cyber Security</span><span>Managing Principal Consultant</span><span>Principal OT Cyber Security Consultant</span><span>Lead / Principal OT Cyber Security Architect</span><span>OT Security Officer</span><span>Department Manager &amp; Engineering Leader</span></div>
</aside>
</div>
</section><section class="reveal" id="leadership">
<div class="section-kicker">02. What He Can Own</div>
<h2 class="section-title">From Board-Level Direction to Delivery Oversight</h2>
<p class="section-copy">Arun's background is strongest where cyber security leadership needs to bridge strategy, engineering, commercial delivery and operational risk.</p>
<div class="leadership-grid">
<article class="card leadership-card"><div class="meta">vCISO / Cyber Leadership</div><h3>Set cybersecurity direction and governance</h3><p>Establish security priorities, governance, risk ownership, executive reporting and improvement roadmaps, providing experienced cyber leadership across both enterprise and operational environments.</p></article>
<article class="card leadership-card"><div class="meta">OT Security Strategy</div><h3>Turn risk into a practical security programme</h3><p>Develop OT security strategy, target-state architecture, remediation priorities and implementation plans aligned with operational criticality, business risk and regulatory expectations.</p></article>
<article class="card leadership-card"><div class="meta">Architecture &amp; Technical Authority</div><h3>Provide senior design and assurance oversight</h3><p>Lead architecture decisions across segmentation, zones and conduits, secure remote access, industrial networking, supplier integration, hardening, threat detection and resilience.</p></article>
<article class="card leadership-card"><div class="meta">Risk &amp; Regulatory Assurance</div><h3>Translate standards and regulation into workable controls</h3><p>Lead IEC 62443, NIS/NIS2, NCSC CAF, NIST and ISO 27001-aligned assurance, while supporting EU Cyber Resilience Act readiness through product-security governance, vulnerability handling, supplier assurance and lifecycle security.</p></article>
<article class="card leadership-card"><div class="meta">Programme &amp; Transformation Leadership</div><h3>Lead multi-workstream security improvement</h3><p>Coordinate security, network and engineering workstreams, suppliers and stakeholders across complex programmes, with clear reporting on progress, dependencies, risks and residual exposure.</p></article>
<article class="card leadership-card"><div class="meta">Commercial &amp; Practice Leadership</div><h3>Build teams, services and client capability</h3><p>Support pre-sales, proposals, service development, recruitment, resource planning, P&amp;L and capability building, drawing on previous leadership of consulting and engineering teams.</p></article>
</div>
</section><section class="reveal" id="sectors">
<div class="section-kicker">03. Selected Sector Experience</div>
<h2 class="section-title">Experience Across Critical Infrastructure and Industrial Operations</h2>
<p class="section-copy">The emphasis here is on the operating environments and security problems Arun has handled, rather than reproducing a job-by-job employment history.</p>
<div class="sector-showcase">
